#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:16
msgid ""
"Show the [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation) that "
"results from evaluating the Hello package:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:19
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix derivation show nixpkgs#hello\n"
"{\n"
"  \"/nix/store/s6rn4jz1sin56rf4qj5b5v8jxjm32hlk-hello-2.10.drv\": {\n"
"    …\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:28
msgid ""
"Show the full derivation graph (if available) that produced your NixOS "
"system:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:35
msgid "Print all files fetched using `fetchurl` by Firefox's dependency graph:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:44
msgid ""
"Note that `.outputs.out.hash` selects _fixed-output derivations_ "
"(derivations that produce output with a specified content hash), while `.env."
"urls` selects derivations with a `urls` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:48
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:50
msgid ""
"This command prints on standard output a JSON representation of the [store "
"derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s to which "
"[_installables_](./nix.md#installables) evaluate."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:53
msgid ""
"Store derivations are used internally by Nix. They are store paths with "
"extension `.drv` that represent the build-time dependency graph to which a "
"Nix expression evaluates."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:57
msgid ""
"By default, this command only shows top-level derivations, but with `--"
"recursive`, it also shows their dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-show.md:62
msgid ""
"`nix derivation show` outputs a JSON map of [store path](../../store/store-"
"path.md)s to derivations in JSON format. See [the manual](../../protocols/"
"json/derivation/index.md) for a documentation of this format."
msgstr ""

